.2 V cut-off; Stage-5 true DFT/MD endorsement of electrolyte oxidation stability before production (not executed in this run) |\n| 4 | Insufficient capacity / energy density for grid application | ED below dispatch requirement or capacity short | ED 447.12 Wh/kg vs 327.18 contract threshold → margin +119.9 Wh/kg (+37 %); 1C capacity 5.0648 Ah vs 5.0 Ah nominal | medium | low | None required (margin); retain architecture when scaling |\n| 5 | Excessive SEI growth over long cycling | continuous electrolyte reduction at anode | SEI 393.00 nm @ 500 cyc vs 550 nm threshold (SEI-k ×0.2 and V̄ ×0.5 coating bridge in design); per-cycle capacity in SEI-only model decays strongly (0.0123 Ah @ 500) | medium | low | SEI-suppressing coating assumed in bridge (estimate-class values) must be validated by physically coated-anode cycling; SEI-thickness measurement at 100/500 cyc in physical build |\n\n## Conclusion\n\nHighest-risk item: **#1 — 4C plating margin (+44 mV) under aged-cell conditions**, followed by **#2 fast-charge heating at 45 °C ambient**. Both mitigations (transport formulation, fine particles, porosity; cooling escalation) are already implemented in the proposed design **at fresh-cell level**; the residual risk is their erosion with aging, which the SEI-only model cannot fully resolve — flagged as the top two physical-validation gates. Items 3–5 have medium/low occurrence on simulation signals."}
